WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.211
In under two minutes, you will close voting and announce the winners.

00:00:04.211 --> 00:00:05.300
We start on the map.

00:00:06.201 --> 00:00:09.533
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.283 --> 00:00:13.705
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.705 --> 00:00:16.195
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.195 --> 00:00:17.541
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.291 --> 00:00:21.507
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:22.159
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.685 --> 00:00:28.180
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.398
See the three dots?

00:00:29.398 --> 00:00:29.946
Tap them.

00:00:31.554 --> 00:00:33.516
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.213 --> 00:00:35.842
Tap Mine.

00:00:35.842 --> 00:00:37.791
These are the contests you run.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.489
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:42.857
This is your dashboard.

00:00:44.741 --> 00:00:45.499
Tap Results.

00:00:45.499 --> 00:00:48.178
It shows who would win if you announced today.

00:00:49.987 --> 00:00:52.530
Tap Download results to save a spreadsheet.

00:00:54.727 --> 00:00:58.384
When voting is over, tap Close voting and announce winners.

00:01:00.162 --> 00:01:03.886
It asks you to tap again, because this cannot be undone.

00:01:03.886 --> 00:01:04.800
Tap it again.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.107
Everyone is emailed.

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:11.454
To see what everyone sees, tap See it as voters do.

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:16.155
The winners keep a crown on the contest page.

00:01:46.779 --> 00:01:49.391
Next up: Read your contest activity.
